Team Lead Product Design (Service) at Company.  UPSTARS – продуктова IT-компанія, з якою злітають і люди, і бренди. Наш основний фокус – технологічні рішення та B2B-послуги для міжнародних клієнтів. Запускаємо зіркові проєкти у сфері iGaming, які отримують визнання та найвищі оцінки профільних рейтингів ✨  І так, підтримувати легальний та прозорий ринок України – це маст хев, тому третіми в країні отримали B2B-ліцензію на надання послуг у сфері азартних ігор.  У 2026 ми активно масштабуємо і проєкти, і дрім тім. Тому для підсилення Design Human-Centered департаменту шукаємо  Team Lead Product Design (Service).   ✅  Твої майбутні задачі:   
  формувати дизайн-стратегію й цілі команди разом із продуктом;  
  керувати командою 15+ людей через супервізорів;  
  налаштувати операційні метрики команди й ухвалювати рішення на їхній основі;  
  працювати з продуктовими й дизайн-метриками;  
  налаштувати процес A/B-тестування разом із продуктом і аналітикою;  
  розвивати дизайн-систему: модель власності, governance, adoption, взаємодія з розробкою;  
  будувати end-to-end процес: вхідна задача, discovery й дослідження, дизайн, handoff, контроль якості реалізації, оцінка після релізу;  
  співпрацювати з Product Managers, дослідниками, аналітиками, розробкою, CRM і Marketing;  
  захищати дизайн-рішення перед стейкхолдерами через потреби користувачів, дані й бізнес-ефект;  
  забезпечувати якість, доступність і зрозумілість інтерфейсів.  
  💪  Твої скіли:   
  7+ років у Product Design / UX/UI, з них 3+ роки в управлінні командою в продукті;  
  досвід керування командою від 10–15 людей, зокрема через лідів, супервізорів чи менеджерів;  
  наявні приклади впливу дизайну на продуктові метрики: baseline, зміна, спосіб вимірювання;  
  досвід налаштування операційних метрик дизайн-команди;  
  експертиза побудови процесу A/B-тестування або системної участі дизайну в експериментах;  
  досвід роботи з дизайн-системами на масштабі (кілька продуктів чи платформ), побудова governance і процесів;  
  сильне продуктове мислення: пріоритизація, trade-offs, аргументація даними;  
  розуміння UX-досліджень, information architecture, interaction design, mobile-first;  
  впевнене володіння Figma, компонентним підходом, досвід співпраці з інженерними командами;  
  досвід презентацій флоу, ідей, результатів для керівництва.  
  🤞  Бажано, але не критично:   
  досвід у digital entertainment, gaming, streaming чи інших high-engagement B2C-продуктах;  
  робота з кількома продуктами чи брендами на одній платформі;  
  Motion

Directeur(trice) de la Direction Digital, Data et IA (DDIA) H/F at Orange Business.  Votre rôle  Digital Services France (DSF) crée une nouvelle Direction nommée Direction Digital, Data et IA (DDIA), en charge de porter la stratégie, le portfolio d'offres, les opérations mutualisées et la performance économique des activités Digital, Data et IA de DSF (à l’exception des activités Microsoft portées par la Direction Expertime). Cette direction est composée d’environ 330 salariés en France, au Maroc et à l’Ile Maurice.  Dans le cadre de cette création, nous recrutons le/la directeur(ice) de cette direction, rattaché au directeur de Digital Services France et membre du CODIR de DSF. Dans un marché en tension mais porté par l'accélération de l'IA agentique, vous avez pour mission de redynamiser la stratégie DDIA, de structurer une gouvernance claire et lisible, et de porter le retour à une croissance profitable et durable de ce périmètre.  Missions principales  Stratégie, portfolio et gouvernance :  
 Définir et faire évoluer la stratégie DDIA (axes de développement, choix de partenaires stratégiques) en cohérence avec la stratégie globale de DSF ; 
 Structurer le portfolio d'offres Digital, Data et IA (Data/IA, Confiance et numérique responsable, Expérience Client/Employé/Opérationnelle, produits digitaux), garantir une déclinaison homogène des offres (dont les produits digitaux) sur l'ensemble du territoire, en lien avec les Régions et les Agences Conseil &amp; Expertise et piloter une vision consolidée. Structurer et clarifier la gouvernance de la direction DDIA, à l'image des dispositifs existants pour les activités Cloud et Microsoft. 
  Pilotage économique :  
 Porter la responsabilité primaire du P&amp;L des activités DDIA (chiffre d'affaires par offre, marge nationale) ; 
 Définir le budget et dimensionner la workforce interne/externe en fonction des ambitions de développement en collaboration avec les Régions; 
 Piloter l'équation de performance globale en coordination avec les P&amp;L régionaux dont les Régions de DSF sont garantes 
  Management et animation des équipes :  
 Piloter les Départements Portfolio, Avant-Vente, Opérations Mutualisées et Live Intelligence, ainsi que les activités du Directeur Technique IA et du Directeur Influence IA 
 Animer un lien fonctionnel fort avec les Directeurs Conseil &amp; Expertise en région et la Direction La Fabrique, afin qu'ils contribuent au cycle de vie du portfolio et à la diffusion des innovations ; 
 Manager les Responsables de départements de la Direction DDIA 
  Alignement commercial

Senior Researcher, Human Rights and Artificial Intelligence at humanrightswatch. &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FULL-TIME JOB VACANCY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Researcher on Human Rights and Artificial Intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technology, Rights and Investigations Division&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multiple Office Locations Considered&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Deadline: December 13, 2026&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Human Rights Watch (HRW) is seeking a highly qualified Senior Researcher on Human Rights and Artificial Intelligence to investigate, analyze, and advocate against human rights abuses worldwide related to artificial intelligence. The role of the Senior Researcher will include documenting and conveying the rights implications of various forms of artificial intelligence and other algorithmic decision-making being developed and deployed by governments and private sector actors around the world for exclusion and repression, including &amp;nbsp;information control and censorship and discriminatory decision making, especially in high-risk contexts, for example by law enforcement and immigration authorities. Experience working on the impact of AI or other technology issues in Asia is preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role sits in the Tech and Human Rights team within the broader Technology, Rights and Investigations Division and will report to the Deputy Director based in New York. The Senior Researcher on Human Rights and Artificial Intelligence will collaborate with other team members in the Technology, Rights and Investigations Division, and colleagues in regional and thematic divisions, and other relevant departments of HRW, including media, legal and policy team, and the advocacy department.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will have deep domain expertise, as well as a track record of conducting&amp;nbsp;research and investigations at the intersection of human rights abuses and AI. The role will be based in any of the following locations where HRW has an office, and will be expected to work from the office on an as-needed basis: New York, Washington DC, Los Angeles, San Francisco, Toronto, Sao Paulo, London, Brussels, Amsterdam, Berlin, Nairobi, Johannesburg, Beirut, or Stockholm.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Develop a plan for strategic research and advocacy for influencing the development, applicatio

Forward Deployed Engineering Manager at Auterion. &lt;p&gt;As the Forward Deployed Engineering Manager, you will lead the team that puts Auterion&#39;s robotic systems to work with customers in the field. We build complete systems: vehicles, sensors, onboard compute, radio links, autonomy software, and ground control. Your job is to understand how all of it fits together and to make it work in real missions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead your team through the entire customer engagement, from discovery and integration to field trials and handover. You are not a hardware specialist. You are a systems engineer who can trace a problem across every layer of the system, lead people well, and earn the trust of demanding customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; Mentorship:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead and grow a cross-functional team of Forward Deployed Engineers covering systems integration and software. Hire, coach, and develop your engineers. Build a culture of ownership and proactive problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accountability:&lt;/strong&gt; Keep the bar high for yourself and your team. Work directly with stakeholders across the company. You will have a close relationship with the CTO, CEO, VP of Engineering, and the engineering directors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field Deployment Oversight:&lt;/strong&gt; Own technical delivery of customer deployments in demanding, non-standard environments. This covers system configuration, connectivity, mission readiness, and operation under environmental constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the technical lead for high-stakes customer integrations. Ensure the full system works end to end: vehicle, payloads, onboard compute, communication links, autonomy software, and ground control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field Troubleshooting:&lt;/strong&gt; Diagnose failures across hardware, firmware, software, and communications. Use logs, telemetry, and structured debugging to find root causes fast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the primary technical contact for defense and enterprise customers. Translate operational requirements into deployment plans that account for system performance, link quality, power, and mission constraints. Run technical meetings, demos, and field days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feedback Loo

Solution Architect (Anaplan) m/f/d at Anaplan. &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Anaplan, we are a team of innovators focused on optimizing business decision-making through our leading AI-infused scenario planning and analysis platform so our customers can outpace their competition and the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What unites Anaplanners across teams and geographies is our collective commitment to our customers’ success and to our Winning Culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Our customers rank among the who’s who in the Fortune 50. Coca-Cola, LinkedIn, Adobe, LVMH and Bayer are just a few of the 2,400+ global companies who rely on our best-in-class platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt; Our Winning Culture is the engine that drives our teams of innovators. We champion diversity of thought and ideas, we behave like leaders regardless of title, we are committed to achieving ambitious goals, and we love celebrating&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;our wins – big and small.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Supported by operating principles of being strategy-led, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anaplan.com/careers/&quot;&gt;values-&lt;/a&gt;based and disciplined in execution, you’ll be inspired, connected, developed and rewarded here. Everything that makes you unique is welcome; join us and let’s build what’s next - together!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anaplan is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Solution Architect&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to join our&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Services team in Germany&lt;/strong&gt;—a group of expert consultants who are passionate about delivering real, measurable value through Anaplan’s cutting-edge planning platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a key member of our Professional Services team, you won’t just be implementing solutions, you’ll shape the future of enterprise planning for our most strategic customers. This team partners closely with stakeholders across Finance, Supply Chain, and Sales Performance Management to solve complex business challenges with smart, scalable solutions. From the very first engagement, you’ll have the opportunity to lead design, delivery, and strategic advisory work that drives transformation at the enterprise level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we drive financial transformation, you will be a key player in architecting the future direction of decision excellence in enterprise grade companies across Germany. You will influence and drive a companies planning direction and play a pivotal role in delive

Senior Research Scientist, 3D Reconstruction & Spatial AI at intrinsicrobotics. &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Intrinsic is an AI robotics group at Google aiming to reimagine the potential of industrial robotics. Our team believes that advances in AI, perception and simulation will redefine what’s possible for industrial robotics in the near future – with software and data at the core.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make industrial robotics intelligent, accessible, and usable for millions more businesses, entrepreneurs, and developers. We are a dynamic team of engineers, roboticists, designers, and technologists who are passionate about unlocking the creative and economic potential of industrial robotics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;em&gt;Role&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior 3D Reconstruction and Spatial AI Engineer, you will own the development of the geometric and semantic perception stacks that power our physical AI framework. You will design real-time systems that enable our robots to translate unstructured, dynamic 3D environments into structured, queryable world models - seamlessly linking high-level task planners (such as VLM/VLA models) directly to robust, low-level manipulation and grasp policies in Flowstate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;em&gt;How your work moves the mission forward&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deploy real-time spatial perception and state estimation pipelines using both in-house models like Gemini/Gemma and open source models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build multi-sensor fusion pipelines integrating RGB-D, stereo cameras, and IMU data into dense spatial representations (ex: point clouds, neural occupancy grids, or implicit signed distance function fields)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ground high-level semantic concepts into 3D geometric structures. This means building queryable, object-centric 3D scene graphs that map not just where an object is, but what it is, and its relationship to the other objects, and its functional properties&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate open-vocabulary vision language models (ex: CLiP based visual descriptors, DINOv2) into 3D metric space to allow the robot to reason about natural language instructions (ex: ‘pick up the half-eaten apple and put it in the trash bin’)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop learning-based spatial models (such as 3D Diffusion Policies) that utilize 3D point clouds to predict conti

Senior Backend Engineer - Nodejs/Typscript at emnify. &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&quot;The-team-and-your-Role:&quot; data-local-id=&quot;ba1876c8-0e3e-48c2-adf7-f7866f5b80f5&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;917&quot;&gt;Your Role:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;944&quot; data-local-id=&quot;b78cb1ed-3088-4d3d-a1ea-5c144273a801&quot;&gt;As a part of the larger Engineering department, the Platform team plays a crucial role in enhancing &lt;mark id=&quot;a843d743-e995-4fde-8833-8956849563a2&quot; class=&quot;css-100s7ye&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-mark-type=&quot;annotation&quot; data-mark-annotation-type=&quot;inlineComment&quot; data-id=&quot;a843d743-e995-4fde-8833-8956849563a2&quot; data-mark-annotation-state=&quot;resolved&quot; data-has-focus=&quot;false&quot; data-is-hovered=&quot;false&quot;&gt;emnify&lt;/mark&gt; competitive edge by improving developer experience to increase development efficiency and scale productivity.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1164&quot; data-local-id=&quot;d8b983b4-8e59-4c90-9b16-e993879da76a&quot;&gt;You will join a growing team, fostering empathy and a collaboration mindset to ensure continuous improvement of development experience at emnify. The Platform team provides, &lt;mark id=&quot;a2e30a38-7ad2-4ffa-8a9f-850c04b16764&quot; class=&quot;css-100s7ye&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-mark-type=&quot;annotation&quot; data-mark-annotation-type=&quot;inlineComment&quot; data-id=&quot;a2e30a38-7ad2-4ffa-8a9f-850c04b16764&quot; data-mark-annotation-state=&quot;resolved&quot; data-has-focus=&quot;false&quot; data-is-hovered=&quot;false&quot;&gt;in addition &lt;/mark&gt;to the centrally managed infrastructure used by all the teams for observability and CI/CD, consultation, SME services, and hands-on support to the engineering teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1518&quot; data-local-id=&quot;42f1384d&quot;&gt;As the &lt;mark id=&quot;e7ac6177-c94f-45e6-a5c9-07f04601b5f3&quot; class=&quot;css-100s7ye&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-mark-type=&quot;annotation&quot; data-mark-annotation-type=&quot;inlineComment&quot; data-id=&quot;e7ac6177-c94f-45e6-a5c9-07f04601b5f3&quot; data-mark-annotation-state=&quot;resolved&quot; data-has-focus=&quot;false&quot; data-is-hovered=&quot;false&quot;&gt;authority on K8s and CI/CD, you will guide infrastructure engineers in best practices&lt;/mark&gt; for K8s, Jenkins, and GitHub Actions, c
